rong immune  response against both the omicron ba1  and the original sars kobe 2 virus  strains  while the vaccine was designed to more  specifically target the omicron ba1  subvariant we know that this vaccine  also generates a good immune response  against the omicron subvariants ba4 and  ba5 that have more recently emerged  health canada is currently reviewing a  submission from pfizer buying tech for a  bivalent vaccine that also targets the  original stars kovi ii strain as well as  the omicron ba1 subvariant  to ensure we have as many options as  possible for dealing with current and  future variants we have reached out to  both visor biotech and moderna to  request that they file submissions for  vaccines specifically targeting the ba-4  and ba-5 subveriance we are awaiting  confirmation on their plans including  submission timelines the national  advisory committee on immunization or  nasty provided recommendations for  booster doses in preparation for the  fall to better protect against an  anticipated increase of covenanting  activity during these months today nasa  has updated this guidance to reflect the  authorization of bivalent vaccines  for adults 18 years of age and older  nasty recommends that a bivalent covet  19 booster vaccine should be offered as  a booster if the bivalent booster is not  readily available an original mrna covet  19 vaccine should be offered to ensure  timely protection it is important to be  aware that both the original and by  valid covet 19 vaccines are effective as  a booster for adolescents 12 to 17 years  of age with moderately or severe  immunocompromising conditions and or who  have biological or social risk factors  that place them at high risk of severe  outcomes from covert 19 based on expert  opinion and the data in adults nasty  also recommends that the bivalent  vaccine may be offered to this  population  individuals who are eligible for  boosters this fall especially those at  increased risk for severe illness fr